{"text": " You wake up in 1928 on a crowded American beach, hot sand, salt air, and everyone's lying in the sun on purpose. Did you know that the famous story that Coco Chanel started the suntan craze is probably a myth? A historian traced it to an unsigned magazine article from 1971. The real reason was work. Jobs moved indoors, so a tan stopped meaning the fields. It meant a day off. Now look in your picnic basket. Bread and apple. The process that made them got its name in 1893. Photosynthesis leaves catch sunlight and turn it into sugar, and nearly all life runs on that. Your lunch is stored sunlight, so in a way are you. The sun used to be something to measure. Now it's the source of every meal. Then in 1954 at Bell Laboratories, a silicon cell turns about 6% of sunlight into electricity. We'd learn that we live on sunlight next we'd learn to harvest it.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 3.02, "text": " You wake up in 1928 on a crowded American beach,", "tokens": [50364, 509, 6634, 493, 294, 1294, 11205, 322, 257, 21634, 2665, 7534, 11, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1320500176800184, "compression_ratio": 1.4712230215827338, "no_speech_prob": 0.006738328840583563, "words": [{"word": " You", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.12, "probability": 0.8672026991844177}, {"word": " wake", "start": 0.12, "end": 0.28, "probability": 0.9894318580627441}, {"word": " up", "start": 0.28, "end": 0.42, "probability": 0.999528169631958}, {"word": " in", "start": 0.42, "end": 0.52, "probability": 0.9648035764694214}, {"word": " 1928", "start": 0.52, "end": 1.3, "probability": 0.991988867521286}, {"word": " on", "start": 1.3, "end": 1.9, "probability": 0.8590517044067383}, {"word": " a", "start": 1.9, "end": 2.0, "probability": 0.9958963394165039}, {"word": " crowded", "start": 2.0, "end": 2.28, "probability": 0.9847356081008911}, {"word": " American", "start": 2.28, "end": 2.68, "probability": 0.9915340542793274}, {"word": " beach,", "start": 2.68, "en